1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,270
This video shows you how to ask the agent about your fleet. It reads the workers and the open issues, as the Status page does, and answers in plain words.

2
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:13,966
Open the agent, and start a new conversation.

3
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,093
Ask a question, as you would ask a colleague.

4
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:31,712
It reads the workers and the exceptions.

5
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:43,653
It answers with one worker on the deployed commit, five rows read by the source and five received by the destination, and no exceptions.

6
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:50,496
Now ask about the records themselves. Say how you want it to find out.

7
00:00:56,440 --> 00:01:05,081
It captures records from the source, as you can in the GUI. When it gets a setting wrong, it says so, and starts again.

8
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:23,590
It stopped early, at thirty-one records, and says so. Most are traffic logs. Three are event logs: admin activity and housekeeping on the FortiGate.

9
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:30,430
Asking changes no configuration. The agent made no branch, and nothing was deployed.

10
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:33,989
Next, you have the agent fix a problem.
